<title>USA: General American boosts buyback program.</title>
<headline>General American boosts buyback program.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>General American Investors Co said Wednesday it will buy back as many as 500,000 shares of its common stock amid a continuation of its current stock buyback program, which began in March 1995.</p>
<p>The company will buy back the shares at a discount of at least 10 percent from their current underlying net asset value per share of $25.58, as of last night, a spokesman said.</p>
<p>So far this year the company has bought back almost 1.9 million shares for about $40.4 million at an average discount of 15.7 percent under the program, it said.</p>
<p>Last year, it said it bought back 1.4 million shares.</p>
